# 📝 Agent Hand-Off & Summary Rule

Whenever you finish a task, successfully edit code, execute terminal commands, or hit a natural stopping point where you require user feedback, you must append an "Executive Summary" at the very end of your response. 

Format it strictly using this exact structure:

### 🛠️ What I Just Did
- Translate all technical tool calls, file edits, and terminal actions into a simple, jargon-free bulleted list.
- Explain *why* the changes were made using plain, accessible language.
- Explicitly list any new files created, packages installed, or structural changes made.

### 🔍 Next Steps & Verification
- Provide 1-2 incredibly simple, step-by-step instructions on how the user can test, run, or verify the changes you just completed.
